  "discussion": "Surf along north-facing shores will rise to near or slightly above seasonal average as a moderate, medium-period north-northwest swell peaks overnight into early Sunday. As this swell declines on Monday, a long-period northwest swell will arrive. This swell will generate moderate surf along north- and west-facing shores through Wednesday. Then a small north-northeast swell will be possible during the second half of next week. A series of small overlapping south-southwest swells will push surf along south-facing shores back to around seasonal average through early next week. A larger south-southwest swell may push surf slightly above seasonal average late next week. Surf along most east-facing shores will be small through early next week, but areas exposed to wrapping northerly swells will experience periods of moderate surf. East-facing shores should also see a bump in surf if the north-northeast swell materializes during the latter half of next week.",
